# URLs `ci-linkcheck` must not report, as regular expressions, one per line.
#
# The list is short and each entry says why it is here. An exclusion is a promise
# that nothing behind it can rot in a way anyone needs to hear about, so a URL
# earns its place by being unreachable *by construction* rather than by being
# inconvenient — a link that merely fails intermittently belongs in the retry
# settings, not here.
#
# Paths are excluded in the workflow instead (`--exclude-path`), because this file
# matches URLs.

# A template, not a URL. `tephpy.io.wyoming.fetch` formats the braces before
# requesting it; fetched literally the archive answers 400 while it is perfectly
# healthy — measured 2026-09-08 against a formatted request answered 200 the same
# minute. Reported here it would be a permanent false positive that says nothing
# on the day the endpoint truly moves, which is why
# `.github/scripts/check_wyoming_endpoint.py` covers it properly instead.
^https://weather\.uwyo\.edu/wsgi/sounding\?datetime=\{datetime\}

# The clone URL the README's installation warning tells a reader to pip-install.
# `git+https://…/tephpy.git@main` is a git transport, not a page; GitHub answers
# the browsable form and this one is not it. geovista excludes its own for the
# same reason.
#
# The `git+` prefix is part of the pattern because lychee keeps it: measured
# 2026-09-08 with `lychee --dump`, the extracted link is
# `git+https://github.com/bjlittle/tephpy.git@main`, so a pattern anchored at
# `^https` matches nothing and the URL is checked anyway. It is optional here so
# that a bare clone URL written somewhere later is covered too.
^(git\+)?https://github\.com/bjlittle/tephpy\.git

# Documentation examples that are deliberately not real. `example.invalid` is the
# reserved TLD for exactly this (RFC 2606) and must never resolve; the localhost
# port is the browser demo's own dev server, which exists only while a reader is
# running it.
^https?://([\w.-]+\.)?example\.invalid
^https?://localhost:

# A per-pull-request Read the Docs preview, written with the number left as a
# placeholder. `check_documentation_links.py` already rejects a preview host
# written into tracked source; where one is *quoted* — in docs-style, explaining
# the rule — it is an illustration and resolves nowhere.
^https://tephpy--
